# Homelab Gitea

Use Git over the existing `gitea-homelab` SSH alias to fetch, branch, and push. Use
`python3 /opt/data/tools/homelab-gitea.py` for Gitea's HTTP API. The helper
reads its scoped token from `/opt/data/secrets/gitea-api-token`; never display,
copy into a repository, or pass that token as a command argument.

Check access before work:

```sh
python3 /opt/data/tools/homelab-gitea.py repo lab-agents-org/colouring-book-v1
```

To propose code, create a feature branch in the checkout, commit, and push it
with `git push -u origin HEAD`. Then open a pull request:

```sh
python3 /opt/data/tools/homelab-gitea.py pr-create lab-agents-org/colouring-book-v1 \
  --head feature/example --base main --title "Describe the change" \
  --body-file /opt/data/workspaces/colouring-book-v1/pr-description.md
```

To open an issue:

```sh
python3 /opt/data/tools/homelab-gitea.py issue-create lab-agents-org/colouring-book-v1 \
  --title "Describe the problem" \
  --body-file /opt/data/workspaces/colouring-book-v1/issue-description.md
```

The repository name is an example; the agent may access only repositories
granted to `lab-agent`. Do not merge a pull request or change repository
settings without the operator's explicit instruction. No Actions, deployment,
or infrastructure administration authority is granted.
